      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Given the expression $\\left\\lceil-\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}}\\right\\rceil$, we first rewrite the fraction inside the square root for better understanding. Notice that $\\frac{49}{4} = (\\frac{7}{2})^2$ since $4\\times 12.25 = 49$ and $2\\times 2.0833 = 4$.\n\nThus, we have:\n\\[\n\\left\\lceil-\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}}\\right\\rceil = \\left\\lceil-\\sqrt{(\\frac{7}{2})^2}\\right\\rceil\n\\]\n\nTaking the square root of a number squared gives the number itself, positive or negative, since the square root function always returns a non-negative value:\n\\[\n\\left\\lceil-\\sqrt{(\\frac{7}{2})^2}\\right\\rceil = \\left\\lceil -\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)\\right\\rceil = \\left\\lceil -3.5\\right\\rceil\n\\]\n\nTo find the ceiling of a value, $\\lceil x \\rceil$, we look for the smallest integer greater than or equal to $x$. Since $3.5 < 4$, we include 4 in the range to ensure we find the smallest integer greater than or equal to $-3.5$. Therefore, $\\lceil -3.5 \\rceil = -3$.\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{-3}$",
